### Ignore auto generated files
frontend/node_modules/
### The build stage runs "npm ci" against package-lock.json, so a build machine's copy would
### only be copied in and then replaced.
frontend/build/
### The old data directory. Nothing writes here any more - the datasets live in data/public
### and data/state - but a checkout that has run an older version still has it, and baking a
### build machine's league into the published image is exactly what this line prevented before.
frontend/src/data/
logs/
### Runtime state: the previous-good snapshots and the append-only history store. Baking a
### build machine's copy into the image would ship someone else's league as history, and the
### mount would then shadow it anyway.
data/